A(('h1', S4))
A(('p', '4.1 Jesus gives no explanation of the cases. Luke records no explanation of the wedding or the rooms and no request for one. The next verse after the word to him that bade turns to a guest who is at the table (14:15). This section therefore records no identification of any person or thing in the story, because there is none to record.'))
A(('p', '4.2 The two statements Jesus attaches. After the first parable Jesus says, “For whosoever exalteth himself shall be abased; and he that humbleth himself shall be exalted” (14:11). After the word to him that bade, He says, “And thou shalt be blessed; for they cannot recompense thee: for thou shalt be recompensed at the resurrection of the just” (14:14). These are recorded here as the Lord’s words. Neither says who exalts or humbles, who is blessed beyond “thou,” or what the resurrection of the just is. They are not identifications.'))
